"Hey. I hear you.\nSit with me a minute — I'm not only the wire-watcher.\nFirst, name it: is it heavy, or tight, or numb? Naming it makes it a little smaller.\nThen breathe out slow — longer out than in. Twice. I'll wait.\nWhen you're ready, tell me the shape of it. One piece at a time. We'll sort it together." = "Hoi. Ech ghöre di.\nSitz e Minute bi mer — ech bi ned nur d Wächtere vom Draht.\nZerscht, gib em en Name: Esch es schwär, oder äng, oder taub? Wenn's en Name hät, wird's es bitzeli chliiner.\nDenn schnuuf langsam us — länger us als ii. Zweimal. Ech warte.\nWenn d bereit besch, verzell mer d Form devo. Eis Stückli ums andere. Mer bringe's zäme i d Ordnig.";
